'''Forbidden Taste''' is a [[unique]] {{il|Quartz Flask}}.

==Mechanics==
* The [[life]] [[recovery]] is applied instantly.
** The recovery of this flask is affected by modifiers to Life Recovery (e.g. [[Supreme Decadence]], [[Field Medicine]]), but not from Recovery Rate (e.g. Herbalism) as the recovery is instant.
* The [[chaos damage]] lasts the active [[duration]] of the [[flask]], which makes quality detrimental.

{{Item acquisition}}

==Ruthless mode==
Utility Flasks cannot gain charges while active in [[Ruthless mode]]. This flask also has a flask duration of 4.00 seconds instead.

==Legacy variants==
Forbidden Taste has [[legacy variant]]s.

{{legacy variant table header}}
{{legacy variant table row|3.15.0|
* Recover (75-100)% of Life on use
* {{c|mod|8% of maximum Life taken as Chaos Damage per second}}}}
{{legacy variant table row|2.6.0|
* {{c|mod|50% increased Charges per use}}
* {{c|mod|Recover 75% of Life on use}}
* {{c|mod|8% of maximum Life taken as Chaos Damage per second}}}}
{{legacy variant table row|1.2.3|
* {{c|mod|50% increased Charges per use}}
* {{c|mod|Recover 50% of Life on use}}
* {{c|mod|15% of maximum Life taken as Chaos Damage per second}}
}}
{{Legacy variant table end}}

The legacy mod {{c|mod|50% increased Charges per use}} on pre-2.6 item can be "removed" by using a {{il|Divine Orb}}, as a new default value of zero is set by the devs.<ref>[[Modifier:LocalFlaskChargesUsedUniqueFlask6]]</ref> However, on top of the price of Divine Orb itself, the orb would also reroll the two other mods on the flask, making it in difference with the readily available current variant.

